Write version.json into flutter_assets, as Flutter's Linux builds do.

`flutter build linux` writes data/flutter_assets/version.json from
pubspec.yaml (or --build-name/--build-number), and package_info_plus reads
the app's version and build number from it. flutter-elinux's asset bundle
didn't write it, so package_info_plus gave an empty version on eLinux. This
copies BundleLinuxAssets.getVersionInfo from Flutter's linux.dart.

Not specific to Sailfish OS; worth offering to flutter-elinux.

